title: The Reckoning
subtitle: The Central Committee meets to decide who failed, and who leads.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 12 and e23_reckoning = 0 and crisis = 0 and congress = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.lead_code = {luxemburgist: 1, offensive: 2, unionist: 3, ultraleft: 4}[Q.leading_faction];
Q.e23_right_blamed = (Q.lead_code == 3 && (Q.german_october == 1 || Q.german_october == 2)) ? 1 : 0;
Q.e23_rk_moscow_left = (Q.moscow_backs == 'offensive') ? 1 : 0;
Q.e23_rk_three = (Q.unionist_gone == 0 && Q.offensive_gone == 0 && Q.luxemburgist_gone == 0) ? 1 : 0;
!}

= The Reckoning

The Central Committee meets [? if kpd_banned = 1 : in secret, in a flat in Berlin with lookouts on the stairs. ?][? if kpd_banned = 0 : in the Zentrale's offices, under police observation. ?] The agenda has one item: the lessons of 1923.

[? if german_october = 1 : The rising was called off at Chemnitz, and Hamburg fought alone. The Left says the Zentrale lost its nerve and left Thälmann's men to die. The Right says the Zentrale saved the party from a massacre, and that the masses would not have followed. Moscow, which planned the October, says both. ?][? if german_october = 2 : The rising was fought and lost. The Left says it was betrayed by hesitation, the Right that it should never have been fought. In Moscow Zinoviev and Trotsky blame each other and agree on blaming the German leaders. ?][? if german_october = 0 and e23_october_done = 1 : The party never rose. Some say it missed the chance of a generation. Others say it is still alive because it did not try. ?][? if german_october = 0 and e23_october_done = 0 : Moscow's October never came to Germany. The party spent the year in strikes and committees, and the Left says that is all it will ever do. ?]

[? if e23_right_blamed = 1 : Brandler and Thalheimer led the Zentrale through the October. Fewer and fewer districts stand by them. ?][? if e23_rk_moscow_left = 1 : The Executive has let it be known that it wants the Left to lead. ?][? if e23_quarrel = 2 : Our own delegates in Moscow voted to condemn the October's leaders, and the Central Committee knows it. ?][? if e23_quarrel = 1 : Our delegates in Moscow stood by Radek and the retreat, and some members of the Central Committee are grateful. ?] [? if e23_rk_three = 1 : Between the two camps a middle group is forming around Wilhelm Pieck, Hermann Remmele and Hugo Eberlein. ?]

The Central Committee will vote on the lessons of 1923, and whoever wins the vote leads the party into 1924. Which resolution does the Zentrale put its name to?

- @right: Brandler's resolution: the retreat was right.
- @left: The Left's resolution: the Zentrale failed the revolution.
- @middle: The middle group's resolution: both were wrong.

@right
subtitle: The Right's defence of its record. [? if e23_right_blamed = 1 : An uphill fight. ?]
view-if: unionist_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_rk_backing = 'unionist';
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

- @open: The Central Committee meets.

@left
subtitle: The Left's indictment. Moscow is likely to approve.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_rk_backing = 'offensive';
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
if (Q.leading_faction != 'offensive') { Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 6; }
!}

- @open: The Central Committee meets.

@middle
subtitle: The centre's compromise. It needs one of the camps to come over.
view-if: luxemburgist_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_rk_backing = 'luxemburgist';
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
if (Q.leading_faction != 'luxemburgist') { Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 4; }
!}

- @open: The Central Committee meets.

@open
title: The Central Committee in Session
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
RG.congressStart({
    id: 'reckoning',
    name: 'The Central Committee',
    stake: 'The lessons of 1923, and who leads into 1924',
    sessions: 2,
    positions: ['unionist', 'offensive', 'luxemburgist'],
    backing: Q.e23_rk_backing,
    kind: 'leadership',
    mandates: 'zentrale',
    delegates: 120,
    ownClose: true
});
if (Q.congress_reckoning == 1) {
    // the districts' verdict on the year, before anyone has spoken
    if (Q.e23_right_blamed == 1 && Q.offensive_gone == 0) { RG.congress.swayTo('offensive', 0.08); }
    if (Q.german_october == 0 && Q.e23_october_done == 1 && Q.unionist_gone == 0) { RG.congress.swayTo('unionist', 0.04); }
    if (Q.german_october == 2 && Q.lead_code == 2 && Q.luxemburgist_gone == 0) { RG.congress.swayTo('luxemburgist', 0.06); }
    if (Q.e23_quarrel == 2 && Q.offensive_gone == 0) { RG.congress.swayTo('offensive', 0.04); }
    if (Q.e23_quarrel == 1 && Q.unionist_gone == 0) { RG.congress.swayTo('unionist', 0.03); }
    RG.congress.tally();
}
!}

= The Central Committee in Session

Forty members of the Central Committee and the district secretaries take their seats around three tables pushed together. The Zentrale's members have a vote of their own. [? if congress_ahead = 1 : The first soundings give our resolution [+ congress_votes_for +] per cent. ?][? if congress_ahead = 0 and congress_votes_for > 0 : The first soundings give the [+ congress_leader_name +] [+ congress_leader_votes +] per cent, and our resolution [+ congress_votes_for +]. ?][? if congress_ahead = 0 and congress_votes_for = 0 : The first soundings give the [+ congress_leader_name +] [+ congress_leader_votes +] per cent. As things stand, our resolution would not survive the first ballot. ?]

There will be two sittings, and then the vote.
